<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Valley Mills sits right on the Bosque County line, where the blackland flats give way to limestone hills and the North Bosque River cuts through some of the best grazing ground in Central Texas. Brazos Ridge Fence Co. builds ranch fence here for cattlemen and hay producers who need fence that holds stock, survives river-bottom floods, and doesn't need babysitting. We're based out of Waco, about 20 minutes down Highway 6, so we can get a crew to your place fast.</p><p>Whether you're cross fencing a hay operation off FM 217, replacing a worn-out perimeter along the river, or hanging a new entrance on Highway 6 frontage, we'll walk the line with you and put real numbers on paper. Every job starts with a <strong>free written estimate</strong>, and we're licensed and insured. Call us at (509) 351-8404.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Valley Mills</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Valley Mills Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">Barbed Wire Fencing</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Five and six strand <a href="/barbed-wire-fence-waco/">barbed wire fence</a> is still the workhorse for cattle around Valley Mills. We drive or drill posts to match your ground, whether that's river-bottom loam or the rocky caliche in the hills west of town.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">Pipe Fencing</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Welded <a href="/pipe-fence-waco/">pipe fence</a> for corrals, working pens, and highway frontage that takes a beating from cattle. Pipe holds up along Highway 6 where wood posts rot out and T-posts get pushed over.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">Game Fencing</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">High <a href="/game-fence-installation-waco/">game fence</a> for exotics and whitetail operations in the Bosque County hill country west of Valley Mills. We build 8-foot net wire that follows rough terrain without gaps at the bottom.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">Ranch Entrance Gates</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Custom <a href="/ranch-entrance-gates-waco/">ranch entrance gates</a> and cattle guards for places off Highway 6 and FM 217. A solid entrance sets the tone for the whole property, and it keeps stock in when a delivery driver forgets to latch up.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
